# Line endings for the files whose bytes are recorded, declared rather than left to each
# clone's core.autocrlf.
#
# Without this the same commit is different bytes on Windows and on Linux, which stays
# invisible until something hashes a file. It did not stay invisible: the intake dataset
# stamp records a sha256 per input, those were written on Windows with CRLF, and the CI
# job on Linux recomputed them as LF and reported that the training data had changed.
# Nothing had changed. `provenance.file_digest` now normalises text before hashing, and
# this stops the two representations diverging in the first place.
#
# Deliberately scoped to ml/intake-parser rather than applied repo-wide: this is about
# reproducible hashes, not about imposing a working-tree convention on everyone.
ml/intake-parser/**  text eol=lf

# Never translated, never diffed as text. Listed because `text eol=lf` above would
# otherwise corrupt anything binary that lands under that tree.
*.gguf        binary
*.safetensors binary
*.dat         binary
*.bin         binary
*.pth         binary
*.pt          binary
*.zip         binary
